<report>
<line><title>Sign test</title></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>For <in>sample</in> observations with <in>sample_1</in> on one side:</b></line>
<line></line>
<block name="exact">
<line>Cumulative probability</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>prob_2</in></pval></line>
<line><pval>One sided <in>prob_1</in></pval></line>
</block>
<block name="large"><line><warn>sample is too large for an exact calculation</warn></line></block>
<line></line>
<line>Normal approximate z = <in>z</in></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>p_2</in></pval></line>
<line><pval>One sided <in>p_1</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><b><ci>Exact (Clopper-Pearson) <in>ci</in>% confidence interval for the proportion:</ci></b></line>
<table>
<tr><td><ci>Lower Limit =</ci></td><td><ci><in>lower</in></ci></td></tr>
<tr><td><ci>Proportion =</ci></td><td><ci><in>prop</in></ci></td></tr>
<tr><td><ci>Upper Limit =</ci></td><td><ci><in>upper</in></ci></td></tr>
</table>
</report>
